{"The upsampling eligibility cache key uses Python's built-in hash() on project IDs, which is process-salted and not stable across workers, reducing cache hit rate and making invalidate_upsampling_cache unreliable across processes": 0.9294450879096985, "Upsampling eligibility is computed using the outer dataset module, even when _get_event_stats is invoked with a different scoped_dataset (e.g. widget split paths), which can incorrectly enable/disable the transformation for the dataset actually being queried": 0.4266502857208252, "upsampled_count() aggregates sum(sample_weight), but the ingestion logic derives/stores sample_rate for client error sampling - if events don't actually contain sample_weight, queries will fail or return incorrect results": 0.8815698623657227}